- The fields are decoded through the same types which are used everywhere. An
- [`EmailAddress`](network-addresses.md#email-addresses) must parse, and a
- [`Name`](names.md) must satisfy its rules. The validation of a form is therefore not a
- separate set of rules. It is the type system doing its usual work at the boundary, and a
- failure carries a pointer to the field at fault:
+ Los campos se decodifican mediante los mismos tipos que se usan en todas partes. Un
+ [`EmailAddress`](network-addresses.md#email-addresses) debe poder analizarse, y un
+ [`Name`](names.md) debe cumplir sus reglas. Por tanto, la validación de un formulario no es un
+ conjunto de reglas aparte. Es el sistema de tipos haciendo su trabajo habitual en la frontera, y
+ un fallo lleva un puntero al campo culpable:

= failure carries a pointer to the field at fault:
=
